      "writtenOn": "2023-09-22T18:54:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think the older API version will have a way to pass child shaders into the mesh creation, so it will fail naturally. That is, if the program specifies a `uniform shader foo`, but the call to `SkMesh::Make` doesn\u0027t pass any children, that will generate an error. And the `SkMesh::Make` call that takes children won\u0027t be accessible from the older Android API.\n\nUnless I misunderstand the concern?",
      "parentUuid": "d2faa5b7_45a97cdb",
      "revId": "6f99ba54b5fe91204aaef8713c3e6ff90552313e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
